          "type": "assistant",
          "text": "Now I have a clear picture. Let me give you a direct answer.\n\n## Short answer: this project won't help you build a poker game\n\nThis project (`agentic-development-task-system`) is **not a web app framework or game server**. It's a local Kanban-style dashboard for managing Claude Code development workflows — issue ingestion, task tracking, terminal session management, adversarial review. Think \"Linear + tmux, for orchestrating AI coding agents.\" It runs on `localhost:5173` for a single user and has no multiplayer game primitives, no WebSocket game server, no auth, no deployment story.\n\nYou *could* use it as a **task tracker while you build** a poker game in a separate repo — but it won't host or serve the game itself.\n\n## What you probably want instead\n\nFor an online browser poker game with friends you need a different stack entirely:\n- **Server**: Node.js + WebSocket (e.g. `ws` or Socket.IO) for real-time game state — SSE/polling won't cut it for poker.\n- **Client**: any frontend framework (React, Svelte, plain HTML).\n- **Hosting**: something reachable on the public internet (Fly.io, Railway, Render, or a VPS) — `localhost` won't let your friends connect.\n- **Game logic**: a poker engine (you can write Texas Hold'em rules yourself or use a lib like `pokersolver` for hand evaluation).\n\n## If you still want to use this repo as the task tracker\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/timothy.shee/GitHub/new-tech-monorepo/agentic-development-task-system__ai\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n# open http://localhost:5173\nnpm run ingest -- epic --title \"Online Poker Game\"\nnpm run ingest -- task --title \"WebSocket server skeleton\" --tags \"backend\"\nnpm run ingest -- task --title \"Table/seat UI\" --tags \"frontend\"\n```\n\nWant me to scaffold a minimal poker game project (WebSocket server + React client) in a new directory instead? That's the real path to what you're asking for.",
