d. No test infrastructure exists in this repo for React components (checked: no `*.test.tsx` in `src/client/`). Adding one is out of scope; we'll rely on manual verification.\n\n### Type check\n\n- `npx tsc --noEmit` clean.\n\n### Manual (end-to-end)\n\nRun `npm run dev`, seed sample data if needed (`npm run seed`), open http://localhost:5173.\n\n**Inline editing**\n1. Click a card title, change it, press Enter → title updates on card; drawer reflects same title; React Query refetch leaves no stale copy.\n2. Click a card title, change it, press Escape → reverts.\n3. Click title, blank it out, press Enter → toast error \"Title cannot be empty\"; title reverts.\n4. Open drawer, change status chip via the new popover to an invalid target → toast error from the transition validator; original status preserved.\n5. Edit tags in the drawer (add \"frontend\", remove \"backend\") → persisted, visible on the card.\n\n**Keyboard navigation**\n6. Press `j` repeatedly on the board → selection walks down the first column; stops at last card.\n7. Press `l` → selection moves to Ready column, same (clamped) row index.\n8. Press `Enter` on a selected card → title enters edit mode, cursor at end.\n9. Press `Escape` in edit mode → reverts and keeps card selected.\n10. Press `?` → shortcut cheat-sheet modal opens; `Escape` closes it.\n11. Focus the filter dropdown, press `j` → dropdown consumes it (does not move card selection). Confirms the input guard works.\n\n**Command palette**\n12. Click the new `⌘K` button in the navbar top-right → palette opens.\n13. Press `⌘K` / `Ctrl+K` from the Terminal page → palette opens.\n14. Type a partial title → matches filter in real time; `↑/↓` moves highlight; `Enter` navigates to `/work-items/:id`.\n15. Type a title that doesn't match → \"Create … as a new task\" row appears at the top; `Enter` opens the creation sub-form.\n16. Submit a new task with an epic picked → task appears on the board under Triage, linked to the epic.\n17. Switch to \"Create … as a new epic\"; submit → epic visible on the Epics page and in the epic dropdown in the task creation form next time you open it.\n18. `Escape` closes the palette cleanly from both search and creation views.\n\n**Awaiting-input notification**\n19. `npm run ingest -- set-awaiting --work-item-id <uuid> --awaiting true` → within ≤5s, card shows amber dot; board header chip shows `Issues (1 awaiting)`; browser tab title shows `(1) TS Agent Orchestrator`.\n20. `npm run ingest -- set-awaiting --work-item-id <uuid> --awaiting false` → dot clears; count hides; title returns to normal.\n21. Open drawer for an awaiting task → \"Clear awaiting\" link visible; click it → dot clears without a second ingest call.\n22. Two tasks awaiting simultaneously → count reads `(2)`, tab title `(2) `, dots on both cards.\n\n**Regression**\n23. Drag a card between columns → still transitions; no interference from inline edit mode or selection.\n24. Drag a card within a column → reorder persists.\n25. Existing drawer functionality (comments, sub-items, reviews) unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## Data flow — awaiting-input\n\n```\nClaude Code hook (Stop / Notification)\n        │\n        ▼\n  npm run ingest -- set-awaiting --work-item-id <uuid> --awaiting true\n        │\n        ▼\n  writes work_item.updated envelope to data/ingest/inbox/\n        │\n        ▼\n  watcher → validator → processor.handleWorkItemUpdated\n        │\n        ▼\n  repositories/work-items.ts updateWorkItem sets awaiting_input = 1\n        │\n        ▼\n  (existing WS broadcast on work_item.updated, if wired)\n        │\n        ▼\n  React Query invalidates ['work-items'] → cards re-render with dot\n```\n\n---\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Click vs drag on cards.** The same region is both a drag handle and a click-to-edit target. The existing code already separates \"click\" from \"drag\" via `isSortableDragging`; inline edit plugs into the same guard. The risk is a brief flash of edit mode if the user starts an edit then drags — miti